{
	// Families: protocol family (p-protocol-*: editor-side members such as the session retro),
	// full prompt utilities (p-*), and composition helpers (c-*, e-*, g-*). Mechanical style:
	// prompt-registry-style.md (same directory). These entries do not invoke or write Protodog
	// state.

	// ============================================================
	// PROTOCOL FAMILY (p-protocol-*)
	// ============================================================
	"Mini Protocol: Session Retro": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "p-protocol-retro",
		"body": [
			"<task>",
			"Run a retrospective of this working session: surface how the work went — not what it concluded — and shape the remediations worth carrying forward.",
			"</task>",
			"",
			"<context>",
			"${1:Name the session or portion under retro and any pain already felt; default is the whole session so far.}",
			"</context>",
			"",
			"<instructions>",
			"- Treat this as a short multi-turn working session at the tail of the session under retro. Offer your reading, and treat my corrections as retro material: record a corrected misdiagnosis explicitly so it is not re-proposed.",
			"- Examine where applicable: items that iterated across more turns than their substance needed, and what form — a picture, an example, an experiment, an earlier question — would have settled them sooner; uncertainties that dragged along, with when each surfaced, when it settled, and what carried it; my corrections that reveal a recurring misread; friction with the operating protocol or method itself, distinguished from session-local accident; and what worked — the practices that are the evidence base worth keeping.",
			"- Ground every observation in concrete session moments, quoting or citing the turn, and carry provenance: my statements versus your inference. Do not launder inference into engineer rulings.",
			"- Shape each remediation as a handoff, not an implementation plan: the mitigation's shape, its open points, and where it belongs — session habit, method change, or an amendment executed later in the protocol source.",
			"- Close only on my explicit instruction. Do not persist by default; on request, write the handoff beginning with `Why this document exists`, preserving pain points with their session evidence, mitigation shapes, open points for the implementer, and corrected misdiagnoses.",
			"</instructions>",
			"",
			"<output>",
			"Work conversationally. On explicit close, return the retro synthesis: pain points with evidence, what worked, shaped remediations with their open points, and anything examined and shelved so it is not re-proposed.",
			"</output>",
			"$0"
		],
		"description": "Start a session retrospective mini protocol at the tail of a working session; surfaces churn and dragged uncertainties, and shapes remediation handoffs"
	},
	// ============================================================
	// FULL PROMPT UTILITIES (p-*)
	// ============================================================
	"Prompt: Independent Audit": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "p-audit",
		"body": [
			"<task>",
			"Perform an independent, adversarial, undirected audit of the supplied context.",
			"</task>",
			"",
			"<context>",
			"${1:Identify the audit boundary, exact code or artifact references, applicable repository or domain material, and relevant state.}",
			"</context>",
			"",
			"<instructions>",
			"- Choose investigation paths from the evidence; do not assume a suspected issue or desired result.",
			"- Consider every applicable common dimension: outcome and acceptance; internal and cross-artifact consistency; evidence, verification, measurement, and evaluation integrity; scope, constraints, invariants, authority, and applicable policy; relevant failure, recovery, concurrency, integration, security, data, operability, and maintainability risks; and unnecessary complexity or ceremony.",
			"- State each finding as one falsifiable claim with exact evidence, affected surface, concrete consequence, and `high / medium / low` confidence. Treat inaccessible or unresolvable claims as limitations rather than guessing. Do not invent findings to fill a report shape.",
			"- State inspected coverage and limitations. A clean result applies only to that coverage.",
			"- Complete without an intermediate scope-inventory stop or engineer steering.",
			"- Audit only. Do not remediate or create Protocol plans, gates, numbered audit state, challenges, or acceptance updates.",
			"</instructions>",
			"",
			"<output>",
			"${2:Return the audit report in this session.}",
			"</output>",
			"$0"
		],
		"description": "Run a self-contained independent audit of code or engineering artifacts"
	},
	"Prompt: Audit Prompt Registry": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "p-audit-registry",
		"body": [
			"<task>",
			"Perform an independent, adversarial review of the supplied prompt registry and the immediate harness behavior that materially changes model input or judges model output.",
			"</task>",
			"",
			"<context>",
			"${1:Identify the registry, immediate harness, applicable conventions and references, supported hosts, and explicit exclusions.}",
			"</context>",
			"",
			"<instructions>",
			"- Establish enough of the actual composition and execution path to interpret the registry correctly.",
			"- Choose high-value investigation paths from the evidence. Follow suspected recurring patterns across entries when useful; do not inventory every prompt merely to claim coverage.",
			"- Consider when applicable: instruction conflict or ambiguity; overlap and catalogue cost; hidden dependencies; authority, HIL, and persistence behavior; cross-host divergence with a named mechanism; harness composition, truncation, schema, validation, retry, and evaluation behavior; safety; and material static or repeated token cost.",
			"- State every finding as one falsifiable claim with exact registry or harness evidence, affected surface, concrete behavioral/safety/portability/efficiency consequence, and `high / medium / low` confidence. A style preference alone is not a finding.",
			"- Preserve placeholders, registered structure, authority, safeguards, and output contracts in any proposed rewrite. Identify desired behavior changes separately rather than hiding them in prose.",
			"- Use `keep / tighten / merge / split / rename / retire` only where a disposition is useful; do not force one row per inspected prompt.",
			"- Audit only. Do not edit the registry or harness, create Protocol state, or stop for an intermediate inventory review.",
			"</instructions>",
			"",
			"<output>",
			"Return the audit in this session. State inspected coverage and limits, systemic findings, prioritized atomic findings with exact evidence, and justified catalogue or harness actions. Do not claim exhaustive coverage unless explicitly required and achieved.",
			"</output>",
			"$0"
		],
		"description": "Run a risk-driven adversarial review of a prompt registry and its immediate harness"
	},
	"Prompt: Improve Prompt": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "p-improve-prompt",
		"body": [
			"<task>",
			"Improve the prompt supplied in context without silently changing its behavior or authority.",
			"</task>",
			"",
			"<context>",
			"$TM_SELECTED_TEXT$0",
			"</context>",
			"",
			"<guardrails>",
			"- Preserve placeholders, intended outcome, scope, authority boundaries, safeguards, acceptance criteria, and output contract.",
			"- Remove avoidable ambiguity, conflict, duplication, and text that does not change decisions or outputs.",
			"- Do not introduce roles, lifecycle stages, persistence, or response structure that the prompt does not need.",
			"- Identify any desirable behavior change separately; do not hide it inside the ready-to-use rewrite.",
			"</guardrails>",
			"",
			"<output>",
			"Return a concise diagnosis, the improved prompt ready to use, a concise account of material wording changes, and proposed behavior changes only when any exist.",
			"</output>"
		],
		"description": "Improve the selected prompt while preserving its behavioral and authority contracts"
	},

	// ============================================================
	// COMPOSITION HELPERS
	// ============================================================
	"Prompt: Open Task Block": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "p-task",
		"body": [
			"<task>",
			"$0",
			"</task>"
		],
		"description": "Open a task block; this does not invoke the Task Protocol"
	},
	"Context: Block": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "c-context",
		"body": [
			"<context>",
			"$0",
			"</context>"
		],
		"description": "Open a free-text context block"
	},
	"Examples: Good vs Bad": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "e-goodbad",
		"body": [
			"<examples>",
			"<good_example>",
			"${1:what to do}",
			"<reasoning>${2:why this works}</reasoning>",
			"</good_example>",
			"",
			"<bad_example>",
			"${3:what to avoid}",
			"<reasoning>${4:why this fails}</reasoning>",
			"</bad_example>",
			"</examples>",
			"$0"
		],
		"description": "Insert contrastive good and bad examples with rationale"
	},
	"Guardrails: Open Block": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "g-guardrails",
		"body": [
			"<guardrails>",
			"",
			"$0",
			"",
			"</guardrails>"
		],
		"description": "Open a guardrails block without implied guardrail content"
	},
	"Guardrail: Don't Fabricate": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "g-nofake",
		"body": [
			"- Do not invent unavailable facts, APIs, signatures, methods, configuration keys, commands, or paths. Verify from available sources when possible; otherwise mark the uncertainty and state what would settle it.$0"
		],
		"description": "Require factual verification or explicit uncertainty"
	},
	"Guardrail: Ask Only About Material Ambiguity": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "g-ask",
		"body": [
			"- Resolve ambiguity from the supplied context and available evidence first. Ask up to ${1:3} focused questions only when an unresolved choice materially changes the result, authority, or safety; otherwise state the assumption and continue.$0"
		],
		"description": "Resolve evidence first and ask only about material unresolved choices"
	},
	"Guardrail: Verification": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "g-verify",
		"body": [
			"- Verify the result in proportion to risk. Do not weaken tests, evaluations, validation, cases, or acceptance criteria to obtain a pass; report material evidence, limitations, and actionable failures.$0"
		],
		"description": "Require proportionate verification without weakening acceptance"
	},
	"Guardrail: Independent Session Defaults": {
		"scope": "markdown",
		"prefix": "g-default",
		"body": [
			"<guardrails>",
			"- Resolve ambiguity from the supplied context and available evidence first. Ask only when an unresolved choice materially changes the result, authority, or safety; otherwise state the assumption and continue.",
			"- Distinguish supported facts, derived conclusions, assumptions, and unresolved uncertainty. Do not fabricate unavailable facts; state what would settle a material unknown.",
			"- Follow applicable instructions and stay within the supplied scope and authority. Capability, access, or available tools do not grant permission or decision ownership.",
			"- Preserve existing work and unrelated content. Do not overwrite or discard it merely to simplify the task.",
			"- Do not perform destructive, external, paid, sensitive-data, or difficult-to-reverse actions without explicit authority. When authorized, minimize exposure and disclose the effect.",
			"- Verify the result in proportion to risk. Report material evidence, limitations, failures, and omitted verification honestly.",
			"</guardrails>",
			"$0"
		],
		"description": "Insert domain-neutral safety and verification defaults for an independent session"
	}
}
